  "d20: 🍽️ Katarina carries the day's surplus to the pantry door, thinks better of it, and turns back to the fire. \"It'll only rot in there. We eat.\"",
  "d21: 🍽️ Bridget rests a hand on the pantry door, satisfied. \"No one's going hungry this week. Sitting with the fever cases instead — someone should.\"",
  "d21: 🍽️ Elif taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
  "d22: 🍽️ Petra eyes the groaning pantry shelves and packs light today. \"No point hauling what'll rot. Mending the nets instead.\"",
  "d22: 🍽️ Desmond leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
  "d23: 🍽️ Lillian lingers by the full pantry and laughs. \"Full shelves, full bellies. Mending the palisade today — the fence won't fix itself.\"",
  "d23: 🍽️ Caleb watches another basket arrive and laughs. \"We're feeding the shelves more than ourselves. Not today.\"",
  "d24: 🍽️ Caleb takes one look at the full shelves and unshoulders the pack. \"Leave the wild standing. Hauling water for the cistern.\"",
  "d24: 🍽️ Caleb taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
  "d25: 🍽️ Caleb surveys the stacked shelves and nods. \"The wild can rest. Splitting firewood instead — winter comes whether we like it or not.\"",
  "d25: 🍽️ Lillian taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
  "d26: 🍽️ Katarina rests a hand on the pantry door, satisfied. \"No one's going hungry this week. Sitting with the fever cases instead — someone should.\"",
  "d26: 🍽️ Lillian sets the sharing basket down by the fire instead of the pantry. \"Full shelves don't need my little more.\"",
  "d27: 🍽️ Elif taps the pantry's fullest jar. \"More than we can eat before it turns. Rendering fat instead — the lamps won't fill themselves.\"",
  "d27: 🍽️ Desmond looks at the full shelves and waves off the day's share. \"No more into the store — we eat at the fire, and the shelves keep.\"",
  "d28: 🍽️ Desmond lingers by the full pantry and laughs. \"Full shelves, full bellies. Mending the palisade today — the fence won't fix itself.\"",
  "d28: 🍽️ Caleb leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\""
 ],
